From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: discard EN751221 duplicate PPE keepalive packets

The generation-1 PPE is configured to send duplicate keepalive packets
with the original headers to the CPU. The original packet has already
been forwarded by the PPE, but the EcoNet RX path passes the keepalive
copy to the network stack, allowing it to be routed a second time.

Consume packets carrying KEEPALIVE_DUP_OLD_HDR on EN751221 before they
reach the bind callback or GRO. Check after the xPON OAM handler because
management frames use a different descriptor interpretation. Preserve
normal unbound traffic and force-to-CPU packets, including WHNAT data.

Flow activity is obtained from the bound FoE entry timestamp, so these
copies do not need to traverse the stack to refresh the flowtable.


Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-6
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 10 ++++++++++
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h |  1 +
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
index d44d31500..b37bbab69 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -463,6 +463,16 @@ static void econet_qdma_rx_process_one(struct econet_q_rx *q, u32 cpu_i,
 					q->qdma->qdma->id, skb, &desc.msg))
 		return;
 
+	/* The PPE has already forwarded the original packet. Do not route its
+	 * duplicate keepalive copy through the network stack a second time.
+	 */
+	if (airoha_is(q->qdma->qdma->eth, econet_en751221) &&
+	    get_erx_crsn(&desc.msg.erx) ==
+	    AIROHA_PPE_CPU_REASON_KEEPALIVE_DUP_OLD_HDR) {
+		dev_kfree_skb(skb);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	hash = get_erx_ppe_entry(&desc.msg.erx);
 	skb_set_hash(skb, jhash_1word(hash, 0),
 		     PKT_HASH_TYPE_L4);
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
index 53d9c2e17..3a3bc5ecd 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
@@ -1140,6 +1140,7 @@ struct airoha_gdm_port {
 #define AIROHA_PPE_CPU_REASON_FOE_UNHIT			0x0d
 #define AIROHA_PPE_CPU_REASON_HIT_UNBIND		0x0e
 #define AIROHA_PPE_CPU_REASON_HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED	0x0f
+#define AIROHA_PPE_CPU_REASON_KEEPALIVE_DUP_OLD_HDR	0x15
 
 struct airoha_ppe_host_ops {
 	int (*get_fe_port)(struct airoha_gdm_dev *dev);
